  "summary_en": "South Korea's Road Traffic Act (amended Aug. 2025) sets rules for road traffic, drivers, licensing and enforcement. It contains embodied-AI provisions: definitions of autonomous driving systems and autonomous vehicles, outdoor mobile robots treated as pedestrians with operator duties (Art. 8-2), and driver training for autonomous vehicle test drivers.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines autonomous driving system and autonomous motor vehicle; driving includes using an autonomous driving system.",
   "Outdoor mobile robots (intelligent robots) are treated as pedestrians on sidewalks.",
   "Art. 8-2: outdoor mobile robot operators must control the device correctly and not endanger or impede vehicles or persons.",
   "Exempts devices for developing autonomous vehicle technology from the ban on enforcement-interfering devices.",
   "Addenda require traffic safety education for autonomous vehicle test drivers (Art. 56-3)."
  ],
